     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"With mfa_admin and segmented deployed (all patched_* false), the attacker can still get deep into the network: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user, then escalate_workstation gives admin_workstation. That satisfies pivot_internal despite segmentation, giving reach_internal. auth_appserver then gives foothold_appserver (mfa_user is not deployed), and kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin. However, auth_dc requires NOT mfa_admin, so it is blocked, and it is the only way to get foothold_dc. Without foothold_dc there is no admin_dc. Without admin_dc, dump_dbadmin_dc cannot run, and it is the only source of stolen_dbadmin. Both auth_db and auth_fileserver require stolen_dbadmin, so foothold_db and foothold_fileserver are unreachable, and therefore admin_db and admin_fileserver are too. Both exfiltration techniques need one of these, so exfiltrated cannot become true.\"}"
    }
